 # Release digest builder
 
-Existing action change_ids is exposed through api.dispatch and python cli.py, accepting one JSON object on stdin and writing one JSON result.
+Actions are dispatched through `api.dispatch(payload)` and the `python cli.py` JSON stdin/stdout router.
+
+## Actions
+
+### change_ids
+
+Returns the list of `id` values from `payload["changes"]` unchanged.
+
+### digest
+
+Input: `{"action": "digest", "changes": [...]}` with at most 200 rows, each row an object
+`{"id": <nonempty string>, "category": "added"|"fixed"|"removed", "title": <string>, "internal": <boolean>}`.
+
+Semantics:
+
+1. Rows are deduplicated by `id`, retaining the LAST occurrence and its position.
+2. Retained rows with `internal: true` are omitted.
+3. Output is a Markdown string with nonempty sections in the fixed order `## Added`, `## Fixed`, `## Removed`,
+   separated by one blank line; rows keep surviving last-occurrence order within a section.
+4. Each bullet is `"- "` plus the title with every run of whitespace collapsed to one ASCII space and
+   leading/trailing whitespace stripped; Markdown punctuation in titles is preserved literally (no escaping).
+5. Nonempty output ends with exactly one newline; if no rows survive (e.g. empty `changes` or all internal),
+   the result is the empty string.
+
+Boundaries: 200 rows is the maximum accepted list length; empty input yields `""`.
+Errors: an unknown action raises `ValueError`; the CLI then exits with code 2, prints the error message on
+stderr and prints no traceback. Input objects are never mutated, even on failure. JSON booleans stay booleans.
+
+## Usage
+
+```console
+$ echo '{"action":"digest","changes":[{"id":"1","category":"added","title":"  Add   new  *feature* ","internal":false},{"id":"1","category":"fixed","title":"Fix #2\tbug","internal":false}]}' | python cli.py
+"## Fixed\n- Fix #2 bug\n"
+```
+
+Discover tests with: `python -m unittest discover -s tests`
